---
import FrameworkLayout from '../../layouts/FrameworkLayout.astro';

const sections = ['Overview', 'The Four Dimensions', 'Assessment Process', 'Strategic Implications', 'Best Practices'];
---

<FrameworkLayout title="VRIO Framework" sections={sections}>
  <h1 id="overview">VRIO Framework</h1>
  
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>
    The VRIO Framework is a resource-based analysis tool that helps identify sources of sustainable competitive advantage. It evaluates organizational resources and capabilities across four dimensions: Value, Rarity, Imitability, and Organization.
  </p>
  <p>
    This framework answers the critical question: "Do we have resources and capabilities that competitors cannot easily replicate?"
  </p>

  <h2 id="the-four-dimensions">The Four Dimensions</h2>
  
  <h3>Value (V)</h3>
  <p>
    Does the resource or capability enable your company to create value by exploiting opportunities or neutralizing threats? Resources must help achieve competitive advantage or strategic goals.
  </p>

  <h3>Rarity (R)</h3>
  <p>
    How many competitors possess this valuable resource or capability? Rare resources are those not widely distributed among competitors, creating differentiation potential.
  </p>

  <h3>Imitability (I)</h3>
  <p>
    How easily can competitors imitate or substitute this resource? Resources protected by patents, complex organizational processes, or intangible factors (culture, brand) are harder to imitate.
  </p>

  <h3>Organization (O)</h3>
  <p>
    Is the organization structured and managed to exploit this resource? Internal systems, processes, and culture must support leveraging the resource for competitive advantage.
  </p>

  <h2 id="assessment-process">Assessment Process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Identify key resources and capabilities</li>
    <li>Assess each on the V-R-I-O dimensions</li>
    <li>Classify as: Competitive Disadvantage, Parity, Temporary Advantage, or Sustainable Advantage</li>
    <li>Prioritize resources aligned with strategic objectives</li>
    <li>Develop strategies to protect and strengthen key advantages</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="strategic-implications">Strategic Implications</h2>
  <p>
    Resources meeting all four criteria (VRIO) create sustainable competitive advantage. Those missing one or more dimensions offer varying levels of competitive benefit. Use this analysis to allocate resources strategically and build defensible competitive positions.
  </p>

  <h2 id="best-practices">Best Practices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Regularly reassess as competitive landscape evolves</li>
    <li>Focus on hard-to-imitate intangible resources</li>
    <li>Build organizational capabilities that compound over time</li>
    <li>Invest in resources aligned with core strategy</li>
    <li>Protect valuable resources through patents, trade secrets, and organizational practices</li>
  </ul>
</FrameworkLayout>
